Every permitted tuple in every case has its actual finite inverse origin, and each case is nonempty.

Proof. This is NBP Propositions 9.3 and 15.2, also PCA Definition 4.1 and FCS Proposition 1.4. To check the full image condition, the root and depth-one children of (BPS.5) have branch right children and cannot equal $E$. Hence each depth-two block must be an image. A block is either $E$, with left beta and right alpha, or a pair of images. Thus $a,c$ are images and a nonimage right class must be alpha with its forced beta partner. Whole-class distinctness permits at most one alpha right class. If there is one, no other class can be beta. Otherwise all six are images and at most one is beta. Since beta is the only image leaf, these are exactly the eleven cases. Conversely each case makes all four blocks and their pairings images. Repetition of a partner uses one value at both occurrences. Injective filling gives precisely the complete row $R_*$, and (BPS.3) gives its actual origin. Distinct choices among (BPS.4) realize all cases and avoid any finite list of forbidden values. The target calculation is §2. $\square$

